UPDATE companies SET description='The Airtex Group was founded in 1918 in Minneapolis, Minnesota, as an agricultural textile manufacturer. Over more than a century, the company has evolved into a cut-and-sew specialist serving a global customer base from its headquarters NE.

Today the firm designs, develops, and manufactures custom sewn textile products, handling processes that include cutting, sewing, filling, printing, and weaving. It operates both domestic production in the United States and coordinates offshore manufacturing partners, and reports having produced more than one billion units since inception.

The company’s customer base spans home décor, bedding, consumer bags, pillows, soft seating, OEM components, and window treatments. Long-term relationships are common, with many clients remaining for decades, and the firm emphasizes collaborative partnerships to meet project goals.

Airtex emphasizes its 100-year legacy of in-house design and strict quality control, offering end-to-end services from initial concept through final delivery, and highlights the flexibility of domestic and offshore options to meet project requirements. The company states its unwavering dedication to quality and craftsmanship as a core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cut and sew manufacturing", "Textile design and development", "Custom sewn products", "Filling", "Printing on textiles", "Weaving", "Contract sewing", "Domestic manufacturing", "Offshore manufacturing coordination", "Home d\u00e9cor textile solutions", "Custom cases", "Contract sew programs"], "industries": ["Home d\u00e9cor", "Bedding", "Consumer bags", "Pillows", "Soft seating", "OEM", "Window treatments", "Agricultural textiles (historical)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Domestic and offshore manufacturing options", "Over 1 billion units produced", "In-house design and strict quality control", "End-to-end service from design to delivery", "100-year legacy in textile manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1918 as an agricultural textile manufacturer -> db, /about", "Headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota -> db, /", "Produced over 1 billion units of textile solutions -> /about", "Offers domestic and offshore manufacturing options -> /", "Serves home d\u00e9cor, bedding, consumer bags, pillows, soft seating, OEM, window treatments -> /", "Capabilities include cutting, sewing, filling, printing, weaving -> /", "100-year legacy of in-house design and strict quality control -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The Airtex Group is a Minneapolis, Minnesota-based company that designs, develops and manufactures custom sewn products and textile solutions.", "founded_year": "1918", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/airtex-design-group/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='the-airtex-group' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Cable Guy was founded in 2006 in Scottsdale, Arizona, as a technology integration firm focused on structured cabling and low-voltage systems.

The firm provides end-to-end installation services including structured copper and fiber optic cabling, security and surveillance systems, home and building automation, audio-visual integration, business telephone systems, overhead paging, and CATV distribution. Its technicians hold Certified Fiber Optic Technician (CFOT) credentials, and the company manages projects from design and material procurement through installation, testing, and ongoing maintenance.

The Cable Guy serves commercial, hospitality, education, public safety, healthcare, and residential clients, offering scalable solutions for businesses of any size as well as private homes. Its project portfolio includes office buildings, hotels, schools, government facilities, and medical offices.

