UPDATE companies SET description='The Modern Table Company was founded in 2014 in Oshkosh, Wisconsin, to create unique, eye-catching furniture pieces for clients seeking one-of-a-kind items to enhance their homes. The company operates from a workshop on North Main Street in the Fox Valley region.

The shop produces custom tables and furniture using reclaimed, repurposed, and new wood that is kiln-dried for durability. Materials include domestic species such as oak, ash, hickory, maple, pine, Douglas fir, cypress, and redwood reclaimed from old Wisconsin pickling vats, as well as the rare Australian jarrah. Each piece is handcrafted to order, with the facility serving both walk-in and appointment-based clients during weekday business hours.

Projects range from coffee tables and high-top tables with stools to other custom builds tailored to individual specifications. The business emphasizes a collaborative design process that translates client concepts into functional works of art.

The Modern Table Company distinguishes itself through its curated selection of reclaimed woods, each carrying a distinct history, and its commitment to sustainable sourcing. The limited availability of materials like jarrah, brought to the U.S. in 1900, underscores the exclusivity of each commission.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and fabrication", "Reclaimed wood sourcing and processing", "Kiln drying of lumber", "Woodworking (joinery, finishing, assembly)", "Custom table manufacturing (coffee tables, high-top tables, dining tables)", "Stool and seating fabrication", "Live-edge wood processing"], "industries": ["Custom furniture manufacturing", "Home furnishings", "Interior design", "Residential construction/remodeling"], "materials": ["Oak", "Ash", "Hickory", "Maple", "Pine", "Douglas Fir", "Cypress", "Redwood (reclaimed from pickling vats)", "Jarrah (from Western Australia)", "Reclaimed wood", "Repurposed wood", "Kiln-dried lumber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom, one-of-a-kind furniture built to client specifications", "Reclaimed and repurposed wood kiln-dried for durability", "Rare and exclusive wood species including Australian jarrah", "Handcrafted in Wisconsin using sustainable materials", "Collaborative design process from concept to finished piece"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 in Oshkosh, WI -> db and /", "Custom reclaimed furniture maker -> /", "Materials: oak, ash, hickory, maple, pine, Douglas fir, cypress, redwood, jarrah -> /", "Kiln-dried for durability -> /", "Location: 2346 N Main St, Oshkosh, WI 54901 -> /", "Hours: M-F 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM or by appointment -> /", "Serves residential customers and interior designers -> /", "Collaborative design process -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "handcrafted in wisconsin; custom reclaimed furniture maker", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": ""