UPDATE companies SET description='Thyssenkrupp Automotive Systems of America operates from Chattanooga, Tennessee, as part of the publicly traded thyssenkrupp AG, which is listed on the Frankfurt Stock Exchange and included in the MDAX index. The division traces its roots to the broader thyssenkrupp group’s automotive technology activities, though a specific founding year for the U.S. entity is not publicly disclosed. Ownership remains with the German parent company, and no individual founders are named for this subsidiary.

The company supplies high‑tech components and services to the automotive sector, covering drivetrain, undercarriage, body, and steering systems. Its portfolio includes forged and machined parts such as crankshafts, camshafts, cylinder head modules, damping systems, springs, stabilizers, and complete drive and battery assemblies. It also provides production systems for powertrain and battery lines, integrated car‑body solutions, engine and axle assembly, and development of electromechanical steering systems. The Chattanooga location employs approximately 28,892 people across the automotive technology segment, though facility size and annual volumes are not specified.

The company’s components serve chassis, body, and powertrain applications, with specific references to undercarriage systems, steering gears, and battery assembly for electric vehicles.

Thyssenkrupp highlights its steer‑by‑wire development approach, the use of artificial neural networks to improve steering‑gear quietness, and the cloud‑based IoT platform carValoo for real‑time fleet monitoring as key differentiators. The division positions itself as an integrated partner for production systems and component innovation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Production systems for powertrain and battery", "Integrated car body solutions", "Engine assembly", "Axle assembly", "Development of electromechanical steering systems", "System engineering", "Forging and machining", "Damping system manufacturing", "Camshaft and cylinder head module production", "Crankshaft and motor component manufacturing", "Spring and stabilizer manufacturing", "Steering system manufacturing", "Drive and battery assembly", "Undercarriage manufacturing"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Automotive components", "Automotive body solutions", "Automotive undercarriage components", "Construction machinery", "Chassis systems", "Body systems", "Powertrain systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Unique steer\u2011by\u2011wire development approach", "Artificial neural networks for steering\u2011gear noise reduction", "carValoo cloud\u2011based IoT solution for fleet condition monitoring", "Integrated production systems for powertrain and battery assembly", "End\u2011to\u2011end car\u2011body specialist capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Chattanooga, Tennessee -> db", "Employee count 28,892 -> db", "Certifications ISO 9001, ISO 14001, IATF 16949 -> db", "Capabilities include production systems for powertrain & battery, integrated car body specialist, engine assembly, axle assembly, development of electromechanical steering systems, system engineering -> db", "Products include forged and machined components, damping systems, camshafts, cylinder head modules, crankshafts, motor components, springs, stabilizers, steering, drive and battery assembly, undercarriages -> db", "Industries served: automotive, construction machinery, chassis, body, powertrain -> db", "Website mentions steer-by-wire development, artificial neural networks for steering gears, carValoo IoT solution -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "High-tech components and services for the automotive industry", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "28892", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='thyssenkrupp-automotive-systems-of-america' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tick Tock Energy, Inc. is based in Effingham, Illinois, and was formed in 2006 by brothers Craig, Eric, and Matt Pals. The venture grew out of a family electrical contracting legacy: their father Mike founded Pals Electric, Inc. in 1983, and Eric brought a decade of experience as a journeyman electrician and IBEW Local 146 project foreman, while Craig contributed a background in energy-efficiency project development for Sempra Energy Solutions (now Honeywell) as a licensed professional engineer.

The company designs and installs solar photovoltaic systems for commercial, agricultural, and residential customers, specializing in ground-mounted arrays — fixed, single-axis, and dual-axis trackers — as well as roof-mounted installations. It also provides long-term operations and maintenance (O&M) services, energy consulting, energy management systems, and energy-efficient lighting retrofits. Since its founding, Tick Tock Energy has installed more than 1 megawatt of solar and small-wind capacity and has reduced several megawatts of electrical demand through lighting and other efficiency measures.

Its client base spans commercial businesses, grain and livestock farms, homeowners, non-profit organizations, and public facilities across Illinois, Indiana, Missouri, Iowa, and Kentucky. Notable projects include a 281.6 kW roof-mounted system for a grain farm in McLean, a 700 kW commercial roof array for a refrigerated warehouse in Effingham, a 604.44 kW ground-mounted installation at a rock quarry in Tuscola, and smaller residential arrays for customers served by Ameren and Wayne-White Electric Cooperative.

The founders frame the business around energy independence, arguing that on-site generation shields customers from rising utility costs and inflation. The company assists clients in capturing federal investment tax credits, Illinois Solar Renewable Energy Credits (SRECs), and USDA REAP grants for rural operations.', certifications=ARRAY['Pearl-certified contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and installation (ground mount, roof mount)", "Solar tracker installation (single-axis, dual-axis)", "Operations and maintenance (O&M) services", "Energy consulting", "Energy management systems", "Energy-efficient lighting retrofits", "Solar incentive application assistance (ITC, SREC, USDA REAP)"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Agricultural", "Residential", "Non-profit", "Public facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pearl-certified contractor for residential installations", "Specialized expertise in ground-mounted solar (fixed, single-axis, dual-axis trackers)", "Multi-state service coverage across Illinois, Indiana, Missouri, Iowa, and Kentucky", "In-house assistance with incentive programs including federal ITC, Illinois SRECs, and USDA REAP grants", "Lifetime O&M support for installed solar assets"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Effingham, Illinois -> /about-us", "Founded 2006 by Craig, Eric, Matt Pals -> /about-us", "Family electrical contracting background (Pals Electric, Inc. 1983) -> /about-us", "Eric Pals: journeyman electrician, IBEW Local 146 project foreman -> /about-us", "Craig Pals: licensed PE, energy-efficiency projects at Sempra Energy Solutions -> /about-us", "Designs and installs solar PV systems (ground mount, roof mount, trackers) -> /", "Provides O&M services, energy consulting, energy management, lighting retrofits -> /, /about-us", "Installed >1 MW solar and small-wind capacity -> /about-us", "Reduced several MW electrical demand via lighting/efficiency -> /about-us", "Serves commercial, farm, residential, non-profit, public facilities -> /, /about-us", "Service area: Illinois, Indiana, Missouri, Iowa, Kentucky -> /", "Project: 281.6 kW roof mount grain farm McLean, IL -> /", "Project: 700 kW commercial roof mount refrigerated warehouse Effingham, IL -> /", "Project: 604.44 kW ground mount rock quarry Tuscola, IL -> /", "Residential testimonials with Ameren, Wayne-White Electric Coop -> /, /about-us", "Assists with federal ITC, Illinois SRECs, USDA REAP grants -> /, /about-us", "Pearl-certified contractor -> /", "Mission: energy independence, hedge against utility inflation -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Tick Tock Energy helps farms, commercial businesses, and homeowners take control of their energy use with solar power systems.", "founded_year": "2006", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tick-tock-energy-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Tillett Textiles was founded in 1946 on Manhattan''s Upper East Side by d.d. Tillett, a Harper''s Bazaar writer, and Leslie Tillett, one of the British-born brothers who had been hand-printing fabrics in Cuernavaca, Mexico. The pair lived above their brownstone boutique and custom screen-printing atelier, where they pioneered techniques such as drag box printing, wax resist, layering, and transparent inks to create painterly hand-printed textiles.

Today the company operates a studio in New Jersey where textiles are still produced entirely by hand using the same methods. Artisans mix custom pigment-based inks and print on linens, cottons, blends, and silks using silk screens — many dating to the 1960s — and drag boxes, a Tillett innovation. The offering spans a readily available collection sold through F. Schumacher & Co. and a bespoke service that allows clients to customize colorways, patterns, grounds, and stripe sizes from the historic archive.

The brand has served interior designers and tastemakers since the mid‑20th century, counting Billy Baldwin, Albert Hadley, Babe Paley, Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, Bunny Mellon, and Diana Vreeland among its clients. Tillett fabrics have been used in the White House, the Oak Spring Estate, and are held in the collections of the Museum of Modern Art, the Philadelphia Museum of Art, and the Cooper Hewitt Smithsonian Design Museum.

The company''s stated distinction lies in its philosophy rooted in nature, imperfection, and the artistry of the handmade. As the firm describes it, only the hand can moderate the dialogue between fabric and ink, and customization down to the tiniest detail remains its calling card.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand screen printing", "Drag box printing", "Wax resist printing", "Layering techniques", "Transparent ink printing", "Custom color mixing", "Bespoke textile design", "Archive pattern reproduction", "Customizable ready-made collection"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Luxury residential", "Textile design", "Museum/archival reproduction", "High-end furniture and upholstery"], "materials": ["Linen", "Cotton", "Blends", "Silk", "Pigment-based inks"], "equipment": ["Silk screens (many dating to 1960s)", "Drag boxes", "Squeegees (varied for different effects)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-printed textiles using original 1946 techniques", "Custom colors mixed by hand for each order", "Drag box printing innovation", "Archive of historic patterns and silkscreens dating to the 1960s", "Bespoke customization of colorways, patterns, grounds, and stripe sizes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1946 by d.d. and Leslie Tillett -> db, /about-us", "Origins in Cuernavaca, Mexico with British-born Tillett brothers -> /, /about-us", "Studio moved to Upper East Side, New York -> /, /about-us", "Current studio in New Jersey -> /, /about-us", "Hand-printed using silk screens, drag boxes, wax resist, layering, transparent inks -> /, /about-us", "Custom pigment-based inks mixed by hand -> /, /about-us", "Fabrics: linens, cottons, blends, silks -> /", "Clients: Billy Baldwin, Albert Hadley, Babe Paley, Jacqueline Kennedy Onassis, Bunny Mellon, Diana Vreeland -> /, /about-us", "Designs available through Schumacher (acquired 2024) -> /about-us", "Bespoke and customizable collection -> /", "Techniques demonstrated at FIT and Skidmore College -> /", "Work in MoMA, Philadelphia Museum of Art, Cooper Hewitt collections -> /", "Silkscreens dating to 1960s still in use -> /about-us", "Philosophy: nature, imperfection, artistry of handmade -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, our textiles are made the same way d.d. and Leslie Tillett made them in 1946\u2014entirely by hand. We mix custom colors and using silk screens or drag boxes, a Tillett innovation, we print on various fabrics from linens and cottons to blends and silks.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='tillett-textiles' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Titan Circuits operates from Phoenix, Arizona, as a division of Outroar LLC. The company specializes in high-mix, low- to medium-volume electronic manufacturing services, focusing on printed circuit board assembly for customers across the United States and abroad.

Its core offering is PCB assembly, covering surface-mount technology down to 01005 passives, QFNs, BGAs, and micro-BGAs, through-hole and selective soldering, flexible and rigid-flex circuit assembly, box-build integration, cable and wire harness fabrication, and functional testing. The shop handles prototype runs through low- to medium-volume production, providing turnkey, consigned, and partially kitted supply-chain options.

The customer base spans military and defense (ITAR and SAM registered), aerospace (AS9100D certified, serving aerospace firms), medical (RoHS IPC Class 3 devices), automotive (power and RF boards for autonomous vehicles), industrial (control systems for harsh environments), and telecommunications (RF assemblies including Rogers/FR4 hybrids). Clients range from small startups to large global enterprises.

