UPDATE companies SET description='Toshiba International Corporation (TIC) was established in 1975 in Houston, Texas, as the U.S. manufacturing subsidiary of Japan''s Toshiba Corporation. The company operates from its Houston headquarters with a workforce of 500 to 999 employees.

TIC manufactures low- and medium-voltage motors, switchgear, drives, and controllers. Its product portfolio also includes high-performance motors for extreme-duty applications, hybrid vehicle systems, and power electronics such as uninterruptible power supply (UPS) units and solar inverters.

The company serves the power generation, industrial, and energy sectors, with motors and drives deployed in oil and gas operations, general manufacturing, water treatment plants, and sustainable transportation projects. Its UPS and energy storage solutions provide backup power for data centers, healthcare facilities, and other mission-critical installations.

