UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Bowie, Maryland, Trim Illusion Inc designs and tests its patented automobile trim products in the United States. The company focuses on aftermarket chrome-delete overlays that give vehicles a custom, high-end appearance without the cost of full refinishing.

Trim Illusion produces a range of snap-on trim components including wheel covers, wheel skins, grille overlays, mirror covers, door-handle covers, emblem overlays, window trims, and tailgate moldings. The parts are molded from ABS plastic with a gloss-black finish and are sold as vehicle-specific kits for makes such as Chevrolet, GMC, Ford, Toyota, and more than a dozen other brands. The company also offers complete body kits that modify the entire exterior with a single purchase.

The business serves both professional automotive shops and individual vehicle owners. Its website notes a "Professional Automotive Shop Approved" designation, and customer reviews reference installations on models like the 2020 Chevy Blazer, 2021 Tahoe RST, and 2026 Honda Pilot. Products are shipped directly to consumers and through the company''s online store.

Trim Illusion says its differentiation lies in U.S.-based design and testing of patented products, promising a unique look that stands out on the road. The company emphasizes easy, tape-assisted installation and responsive customer support when fitment issues arise.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automobile trim overlay design and testing", "Chrome delete gloss black kit production", "Vehicle-specific fitment engineering", "Snap-on adhesive installation kits", "Customer support and fitment resolution"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Automotive accessories", "Professional automotive shops", "Consumer vehicle customization"], "materials": ["ABS plastic"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented products designed and tested in the U.S.", "Complete chrome-delete kits for full-vehicle makeovers", "Professional Automotive Shop Approved designation", "Vehicle-specific fitments for over 20 makes", "Responsive customer service with quick issue resolution"], "facts_used": ["Location: Bowie, Maryland -> db", "Certification: IATF16949 -> db", "Patented products designed and tested in US -> /", "Product range: wheel covers, grille overlays, mirror covers, door handle covers, emblem overlays, window trims, tailgate moldings -> /", "Vehicle makes served: Chevrolet, GMC, Ford, Toyota, etc. -> /", "Professional Automotive Shop Approved -> /", "Customer reviews mention 2020 Chevy Blazer, 2021 Tahoe RST, 2026 Honda Pilot -> /", "ABS plastic material -> /", "Complete body kits -> /", "Responsive customer service -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our patented products are designed and tested in the US, to make your vehicle truly unique.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='trim-illusion-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Trivium Packaging, headquartered in Roanoke, Virginia, was founded in 2001. The company operates as a global manufacturer of metal packaging, with 57 locations worldwide and approximately 7,200 employees generating annual revenue of about $3 billion.

The company produces a wide range of metal packaging including two-piece and three-piece cans, aerosols, threaded bottles, beverage bottles, and slugs, ends, and components. Its shaping technologies encompass mechanical expansion, impact extrusion, and blow moulding, complemented by advanced graphic design and printing capabilities. Research and development facilities in France and the United States support innovations such as the Tripod can, SpringLatch closure system, and Easy Peel opening solution.

Trivium serves diverse industries: food (seafood, vegetables, wet and dry products), beverages (water, soft drinks, beer, wine, spirits), coffee (ready-to-drink, instant, ground, beans), beauty and personal care (body sprays, washes, lotions, hair products), health and nutrition (vitamins, supplements, OTC, prescription drugs, infant formula), pet (pet food, care, health), paints and coatings (liquid and aerosol spray paints), and home care and industrial (household cleaners, industrial disinfectants, automotive care). Its customers include global brands seeking sustainable packaging.

The company differentiates itself through a focus on circularity—metal packaging that is infinitely recyclable without quality loss—and an Operational Excellence program that drives continuous efficiency improvements. Trivium also offers end-to-end support from graphics and design through certification, compliance, technical consultancy, and training, backed by more than 25 years of experience in packaging innovation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal packaging manufacturing", "Mechanical expansion", "Impact extrusion", "Blow moulding", "Graphic design and printing", "Technical consultancy", "Certification and compliance support", "Training", "R&D and innovation", "Sustainability consulting", "Packaging design", "Two-piece can making", "Three-piece can making", "Aerosol can production", "Bottle manufacturing (threaded, beverage)", "Component manufacturing (slugs, ends)"], "industries": ["Food", "Beverages", "Coffee", "Beauty and Personal Care", "Health and Nutrition", "Pet", "Paints and Coatings", "Home Care and Industrial"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminium"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Infinitely recyclable metal packaging that stays in the loop", "R&D facilities in France and the US producing innovations like the Tripod can and SpringLatch closure", "Shaping technologies: mechanical expansion, impact extrusion, and blow moulding", "End-to-end support from graphics and design to certification and compliance", "Operational Excellence program driving continuous efficiency improvements"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db", "Headquarters Roanoke, Virginia -> db", "57 locations globally -> /about-us", "Approximately 7,200 employees -> /about-us", "Annual revenue ~$3 billion -> /about-us", "Shaping technologies: mechanical expansion, impact extrusion, blow moulding -> /about-us", "R&D facilities in France and US -> /about-us", "Innovations: Tripod can, SpringLatch closure, Easy Peel -> /about-us", "Industries served: Food, Beverages, Coffee, Beauty and Personal Care, Health and Nutrition, Pet, Paints and Coatings, Home Care and Industrial -> /", "Product types: two-piece cans, three-piece cans, aerosols, threaded bottles, beverage bottles, slugs, ends, components -> /", "End-to-end support, graphics and design, certification and compliance, technical consultancy, training -> /services", "Metal infinitely recyclable -> /about-us", "Operational Excellence program -> /about-us", "Languages supported: English, Spanish, French, Portuguese, Italian, German, Dutch, Polish -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Trivium provides industry-leading expertise in producing and supplying metal packaging for a variety of applications and industries.", "founded_year": "2001", "employee_count": "Approximately 7,200", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Spanish", "French", "Portuguese", "Italian", "German", "Dutch", "Polish"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='trivium-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='TruNorth Solar is a Minnesota-based solar contractor headquartered in Roseville, founded in 2009 by Marty Morud. The company traces its origins to a family farm in Bemidji where Morud, along with college roommate Steve and business partner Dave, built their first array for Morud’s father. After buying out his partners in 2013, Morud became sole owner and grew the business into a full-service installer serving residential, commercial, and agricultural clients across Minnesota and western Wisconsin.

The firm designs and installs photovoltaic systems ranging from rooftop residential arrays to large-scale commercial and agricultural projects, and has completed more than 1,200 installations totaling 26 megawatts of community solar and over 110 commercial arrays. A staff of roughly 30 employees handles every phase in‑house — engineering, permitting, incentive paperwork, interconnection, construction, and commissioning — and operates a dedicated “Life of System” service department that maintains and repairs any solar or storage system regardless of original installer.

Customers include homeowners seeking lower electric bills, businesses leveraging grants such as Xcel Energy’s Solar*Rewards and C‑PACE financing, and farms pursuing energy resilience and property‑value gains. TruNorth also develops community solar gardens that allow subscribers to offset utility costs without on‑site equipment.

Morud frames the company’s mission around environmental stewardship and “honest handshakes,” emphasizing that savings extend beyond money. Membership in the Amicus Solar Cooperative — an invitation‑only national network of independent installers — provides collective buying power and continuous best‑practice sharing, and TruNorth remains the only Amicus member installer in Minnesota.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar PV design and installation", "Commercial solar PV design and installation", "Agricultural solar PV design and installation", "Community solar garden development", "Solar system maintenance and repair", "Re\u2011roofing coordination for solar installations", "System troubleshooting and performance optimization", "Inverter maintenance and replacement", "Battery storage system maintenance", "Permitting, interconnection, and incentive paperwork management", "Electrical inspection and commissioning"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Community solar"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Inverters", "Electrical wiring and connectors", "Mounting and racking systems", "Battery storage systems"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Life of System\" service department maintaining any solar/storage system", "Sole Minnesota installer member of Amicus Solar Cooperative", "In\u2011house management of assessments, incentives, permitting, interconnection, and commissioning", "Certified technicians servicing all system brands", "Local expertise in Minnesota climate and incentive landscape"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 by Marty Morud -> /about", "Headquartered in Roseville, Minnesota -> db", "Installed over 1,200 solar arrays -> /about", "26MW of community solar projects developed -> /about", "110+ commercial arrays installed -> /about", "30 employees -> /about", "Member of Amicus Solar Cooperative -> /about", "Offers ''Life of System'' service for any solar/storage system -> /about, /services", "Provides residential, commercial, agricultural solar installation -> /, /about", "Handles permitting, incentives, interconnection, commissioning in-house -> /about", "Services include re-roofing coordination, system maintenance, troubleshooting -> /services", "Serves customers in Minnesota and western Wisconsin -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "TruNorth Solar is a Minnesota-based solar contractor founded in 2009 that specializes in high-quality residential, commercial, and agricultural solar installations", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "30", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='trunorth-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Truck & Transportation Equipment Company has operated from Jefferson, Louisiana, since 1967. The business began as a final-stage truck manufacturer, taking incomplete cab-and-chassis units of any make and completing them as customized work trucks for customers across the southern United States.

The company''s eight-acre campus on Industrial Avenue includes seven buildings straddling the street: a main shop with twelve work bays, a quick-get-ready shop with five bays, a separate heavy-fabrication shop equipped with metal brakes, shears, and gantry cranes, a full paint shop, and multiple parts and storage buildings. The fabrication shop can produce any truck body a customer requires, while the service department runs twenty-seven full bays for repairs and warranty work. A large on-site inventory supports its role as a Louisiana distributor for major truck-equipment brands.

Customers range from commercial fleets and construction firms to government agencies, municipalities, and first-responder organizations. The company supplies fire and EMS apparatus, police and emergency lighting from Federal Signal, and a sandbagging attachment that mounts to construction vehicles. Its parts counter serves cargo vans, light-, medium-, and heavy-duty trucks, and tractor-trailers.

