 products -> homepage", "Federal Signal police and emergency vehicle lights/sirens -> homepage", "Sandbagging machine for construction vehicles -> homepage", "Service after the sale emphasis -> homepage", "Sales team collective 150 years experience -> homepage", "Financing available -> homepage", "Address 260 Industrial Ave, Jefferson, LA 70121 -> homepage", "Social media icons: Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, YouTube, Yelp -> homepage", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "final stage truck manufacturer", "founded_year": "1967", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/truck/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='truck-transportation-equipment-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='True South Solar was founded in 2010 in Ashland, Oregon. The company began as a solar installation provider for Southern Oregon residents and businesses, establishing itself as a local installer focused on renewable energy solutions.

The company provides commercial solar installations, battery energy storage systems (BESS), feasibility studies, tax credit and incentive filing, solar expansions, service agreements, monitoring support, panel removal and replacement, and warranty claim assistance. Its in-house team handles design through installation, and it partners with ELM Microgrid Solutions for commercial-scale storage. The firm has served thousands of customers across the region over more than 15 years.

True South Solar works with commercial businesses, schools, and nonprofits seeking on-site renewable energy. Clients include organizations with flat roofs or unused land looking to reduce energy costs, gain backup power, or meet sustainability goals. The company also assists with grant funding from the Energy Trust of Oregon and federal REAP grants.

The company says it is driven by a vision of a Net-Zero Rogue Valley and values such as empowering change, sustainability in action, safety first, unwavering integrity, innovation, and creating meaningful careers. It emphasizes local roots, transparent processes, and long-term client relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial solar installations", "Battery energy storage systems (BESS)", "Feasibility studies", "Tax credit and incentive filing", "Solar expansions", "Service agreements", "Monitoring issue resolution", "Solar panel removal and replacement", "Warranty claim assistance", "Free solar consultations"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Education", "Nonprofit"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Battery energy storage systems", "Inverters"], "equipment": ["ELM Microgrid Solutions"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design through installation", "Feasibility studies with Energy Trust of Oregon grant funding", "Tax credit and incentive filing assistance including federal REAP grants", "Free 15-minute monitoring consultation", "Solar panel removal and reinstallation for roof replacement"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 -> /", "Headquarters in Ashland, Oregon -> db", "Provides commercial solar installations -> /services", "Offers battery energy storage systems (BESS) -> /services", "Performs feasibility studies with Energy Trust of Oregon grant funding -> /services", "Assists with tax credit and incentive filing including federal REAP grants -> /services", "Provides service agreements for annual monitoring -> /services", "Offers solar panel removal and replacement for roof repairs -> /services", "Handles warranty claims for panels and inverters -> /services", "Partners with ELM Microgrid Solutions for commercial-scale storage -> /services", "Serves commercial businesses, schools, and nonprofits -> /services", "Company values include Net-Zero Rogue Valley vision, empowering change, sus