UPDATE companies SET description='US Advanced Medical Research, Inc., based in Henderson, Nevada, was founded in 1988 by Dr. Brian Jegasothy, Dr. Lingam, and Alice Thiel. The trio—dermatologists, Ayurvedic practitioners, and cosmetic scientists with over 200 years of combined expertise—created the Hylunia brand to develop clean, anti-inflammatory skincare that prevents inflammaging and slows skin aging.

The company formulates and manufactures its own product line—including serums, creams, lotions, and mists—using plant-based hyaluronic acid, green tea, turmeric, neem, and vitamin C. Production runs in small batches at the Henderson facility to maintain freshness. The operation serves more than 1,000 professional spas nationwide and has sold over 5 million units to date.

Hylunia products target professional aestheticians, dermatology offices, and spa retailers, as well as direct consumers seeking solutions for age-delay, lift and firm, brightening, oily and acne-prone skin, rosacea and redness, and dark circles. The brand is positioned in the professional skincare, spa and wellness, and anti-aging cosmetics markets.

The founders built the company on a prevention-first philosophy, fusing Ayurvedic tradition with modern clinical research to soothe oxidative stress and support the skin''s natural recovery. Every formulation avoids parabens, sulfates, synthetic fragrances, and endocrine disruptors, reflecting a commitment to safety and efficacy that the company says sets it apart.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Skincare formulation", "Small batch manufacturing", "Clean beauty product development", "Anti-inflammatory product development", "Plant-based ingredient sourcing", "Quality control for freshness"], "industries": ["Professional skincare", "Spa and wellness", "Anti-aging cosmetics", "Dermatology", "Retail beauty"], "materials": ["Plant-based hyaluronic acid", "Green tea", "Turmeric", "Neem", "Vitamin C"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small batch production; 5M+ units sold to date", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Small batch manufacturing in Henderson, Nevada", "Plant-based hyaluronic acid in every formulation", "Formulated by dermatologists and Ayurvedic practitioners", "Free of parabens, sulfates, synthetic fragrances, and endocrine disruptors", "Trusted by over 1,000 professional spas nationwide"], "facts_used": ["Company name: US Advanced Medical Research, Inc. -> db", "Brand: Hylunia -> db", "Founded 1988 -> db, /", "Founders: Dr. Brian Jegasothy, Dr. Lingam, Alice Thiel -> /", "HQ: Henderson, Nevada -> db, /", "Small batch production in Henderson -> /", "1,000+ spas nationwide -> /", "5M+ units sold -> /", "Plant-based hyaluronic acid, green tea, turmeric, neem, vitamin C -> /", "Free of parabens, sulfates, synthetic fragrances, endocrine disruptors -> /", "Prevention-first philosophy -> /", "Formulated by dermatologists and research scientists -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We produce in small batches to ensure the freshness of our products in Henderson, Nevada.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='us-advanced-medical-research-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='U.S. Wire & Cable Corporation has been producing cable and extension cords in Newark, New Jersey since 1985. The business traces its roots to 1956 when Alex Folkman founded Flexon Industries on the pillars of quality, service, and family values. Today the corporation remains family-owned and operated under the leadership of Chairman Joseph Folkman, President Warren Swindlehurst, and Vice President David Rauch.

The company operates three U.S. manufacturing facilities and six distribution centers, supplemented by offshore production. Its four divisions — Flexon Industries, Winzeler Couplings & Metals, U.S. Wire & Cable, and Voltec Power & Lighting — manufacture garden hoses, precision metal stampings and ferrules, power cords, extension cords, task lighting, and power distribution systems. Product lines include indoor household cords, appliance cords, cold-weather and oil-resistant extension cords, cord management accessories, and GFCI devices.

Customers span retail partners, distributors, and consumers across the lawn-and-garden, electrical, construction, and automotive channels. Flexon serves professional and home lawn care; Voltec targets electrical and construction markets; Winzeler supplies precision metal components to automotive and other industries.

