UPDATE companies SET description='Uniforce Plastics operates from Conway, Arkansas. The company traces its roots to 1990 when Uniforce Tech was founded as an electronics developer; Uniforce Plastics followed soon after to provide plastics, tooling, wire harnesses, and electrical assemblies for OEMs nationwide.

The shop combines plastics fabrication, tooling, thermoforming, additive manufacturing, and electrical assembly under one roof. Core processes include handmade two-part fiberglass tooling for deep-draw and intricate shapes, automated 5-axis CNC machining and robotic cutting cells, large-format 3D printing up to ten feet with 48-hour prototype turnaround, and custom wire harnesses up to sixty feet long with hundreds of connection points. Production capabilities extend to automated thermoforming, CNC trimming, and full electrical assembly and testing, with tooling lead times of three to five days.

Uniforce serves OEMs in marine, ATV/UTV, heavy highway vehicles and school buses, and agriculture. Marine work includes dashboards, shifters, cup holders, speaker panels, and iceboxes; ATV/UTV projects cover durable plastics, electrical harnesses, and dashboard assemblies; heavy vehicle and bus programs involve electrical assemblies, large tooling, and custom panels; agricultural customers receive rugged plastics and electrical components built for demanding environments.

The company emphasizes integrated manufacturing for maximum precision, citing fast turnaround (prototyping and tooling in as little as 48 hours), consolidated services (plastics, tooling, thermoforming, harnessing, and assembly in one facility), cutting-edge technology (5-axis CNC, robotic cutting, Delta Sigma projection systems), and OEM-ready direct-to-line shipments with customer-specific designs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["5-axis CNC machining", "Robotic cutting", "Delta Sigma 3D projection", "Handmade two-part fiberglass tooling", "Marine-grade vinyl finishing", "Large-format 3D printing (up to 10 ft)", "Rapid prototyping (48-hour turnaround)", "Automated thermoforming", "CNC trimming", "Wire harness assembly", "Automated cut-to-length wire processing", "Electrical assembly and testing", "Quality inspection and measurement", "Direct-to-line shipment", "Custom OEM product development", "Small-batch and one-off production", "Thermoforming and vacuum forming for deep-draw components"], "industries": ["Marine", "ATV/UTV", "Heavy Highway Vehicles & School Buses", "Agriculture"], "materials": ["Plastics (various)", "Marine-grade vinyl", "Fiberglass (for tooling)", "Wire and cable (for harnesses)"], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC machining centers", "Robotic cutting cells", "Delta Sigma 3D projection systems", "Large-format 3D printers (up to 10 ft)", "Automated thermoforming equipment", "CNC trimming machines", "Automated cut-to-length wire processing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "48 hours for 3D printed prototypes; 3-5 days for tooling", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prototyping and tooling in as little as 48 hours via in-house 3D printing", "Plastics, tooling, thermoforming, harnessing, and assembly under one roof", "5-axis CNC machining, robotic cutting cells, and Delta Sigma projection systems", "Direct-to-line shipments and customer-specific designs for seamless OEM integration", "Every wire harness tested during assemb